    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d612">

                <pb facs="0738" n="653" xml:id="pg653"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.001W64/104: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-11-21T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 21,
                                1918, 7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>56. For Colonel House: Referring to your No. 121, it is my own feeling that there
                    are many serious disadvantages in having the Kaiser so near his former kingdom
                    and so near also to the centers of intrigue. I am at a loss to suggest what
                    course ought to be taken, but I think that Holland will find him an exceedingly
                    inconvenient and even dangerous guest. Woodrow Wilson.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
